  "description": "Two conflict stories (paint against stain) are reviewed with no_change at Wednesday 10:00. A-601 changes Door 101 to brown-paint at the same instant, with no @after evidence: the related story's begin act cites that A-601 Assertion, the disagreeing document's statement, and lists the review in tied; at the instant itself whether it has begun is ambiguous. A-601's Tuesday brown-paint for Door 102, recorded after the Wednesday review, opens a related story whose interval begins at the review's effective time: its begin act cites the review, with no tie, and a Tuesday frame shows it not started.",
  "note": "7.6.4: for `disagreement`, \"Where the interval begins at a review's effective time because the change that opened it occurred before the review (7.3.1), it is that review. Where that change is tied with the review's effective time, with no `@after` evidence ordering them (7.3.1, 7.3.6), the record is that side Assertion, the disagreeing document's statement, and the review is listed in `tied` (7.6.6).\"",
